      "message": "Can you say a little bit about what you are planning to do for this?\n\nAs it currently stands, the bounds below that use `::max()` for the upper limit are not always correct. Take for example a loop with the form:\n```\nfor (var i \u003d 5i; i \u003e 0i; i--) {\n}\n```\nFor this loop variable you\u0027d assign the bounds `[5, INT64_MAX]`, but the actual bounds are `[1, 5]` since it decrements instead of increments.\n\nIs the plan to do all of the same checks that we do in `LoopAnalysis` to check for the simple inc/dec by `1` pattern, and fail to produce any bounds if it doesn\u0027t match that exact pattern?",
